WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.232
The browser practice database is intentionally small.

00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:07.507
It includes sales, admissions, survey responses, and web events.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:11.787
These are not meant to be big-data examples.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:17.622
They are meant to help you practice SQL logic before running the same kind of logic in Spark.

00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:21.812
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:26.982
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:30.487
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:34.782
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:41.507
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:45.687
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:45.687 --> 00:00:50.294
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
